        "shortTitle": "Section 2",
        "longTitle": "Gastro-oesophageal disease (GERD)",
        "text": "ACID RELATED CONDITIONS\nGastro-oesophageal disease (GERD)\nPresenting as heartburn, acid regurgitation and sometimes difficulty or pain on\nswallowing, occasionally with a cough and/or a hoarse voice.\nGeneral measures:\nLifestyle modifications are important: weight reduction, elevation of head of bed,\navoidance of tight clothes, stooping, large meals, and food triggers that patient\nsuspects (chocolate, colas, coffee, fatty or spicy foods). No meals or drink for 3\nhours preceding bedtime.\nMild symptoms:\nMedicine\nCodes\nAdult dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nmagnesium trisilicate &\naluminium\nhydroxide\npo\nC\nN\n20ml or 2\ntablets\nat least 4 times a\nday\nas required\nModerate symptoms:\nn\nMedicine\nCodes\nAdult dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nadd\n*omeprazole po\nB\nE\n20mg\nonce daily\n2 months\n* Omeprazole to be taken 30 minutes BEFORE meals.\nSevere symptoms: If no response to above, give:\nMedicine\nCodes\nAdult dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nomeprazole po\nB\nE\n20mg\ntwice a day\n6-8 weeks\nNote: NSAIDs, CCBs, nitrates, theophylline can worsen reflux. Avoid use if\nreflux occurs. Combination treatment is less effective than increasing the dose of\nPPI.\n\nHeartburn or pain on swallowing unresponsive to treatment, presence of\ndysphagia, weight loss should be referred to specialist. (Also see odynophagia\nbelow)\nOdynophagia: (Pain on swallowing)\nWhen pain on swallowing is recent in onset and with no heartburn consider\noesophagitis\nfrom\npill\ningestion,\nHIV\ncomplicated\nby\ncandidiasis,\nviral\noesophagitis and malignancy. Empirical anti-fungal agent in HIV infected patients\nor if there are other potential causes of immunosuppression. Early referral for\nintractable cases."
