        "shortTitle": "Section 10",
        "longTitle": "SYSTEMIC LUPUS ERYTHEMATOSUS (SLE)",
        "text": "Medicine\nCodes\nAdult dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nfolate po\nB\nV\n5-10mg\n2-3 times per week\nreview\n*Give folate 5-10mg 2-3 times per week with the methotrexate- give folate on\na different day when not taking methotrexate.\nAssess disease activity using a Clinical Disease Activity score at 3 monthly\nvisits to determine if the methotrexate dose needs to be increased.\nOral, low maintenance dose prednisolone can be added where indicated for a\nlimited period:\nMedicine\nCodes\nAdult dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nprednisolone po\nB\nV\n5– 10mg\nonce a day\nlimited\nperiod\n( 2-3 months)*\nor\nmethylprednisol\none iv\nA\nV\n40-80mg\nIM\nonce only(stat)\nNote: Best results are achieved with combination of medicines.\n*Prednisolone is used for a while whilst waiting for the DMRARDs e.g.\nmethotrexate or hydroxychloroquine to start working.\nSYSTEMIC LUPUS ERYTHEMATOSUS (SLE)\nRefer to a higher level for diagnosis and initial treatment. There will be need to\nexclude other organ involvement e.g. renal disease. Sun-exposure should be\navoided as much as possible by using broad-brimmed hats and umbrellas.\nIf severe skin or joint lesions, add:\nMedicine\nCodes\nAdult dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nhydroxychloroquine\npo\nS\nE\n400mg\nonce a day\ncontinual/ review\nor\nchloroquine\nS\nE\n300mg\nonce a day\ncontinual/review\nIn severe disease with complications e.g. renal, neurological, vascular or\nhaematological add prednisolone in high doses as well as immunosuppressive\nmedicines:"
