        "shortTitle": "Section 6",
        "longTitle": "Anti-depressants and Neuroleptics",
        "text": "Corticosteroids\nThese are useful in reducing pain from nerve compression, tumour related oedema\ne.g. liver capsule pain, nerve compression and raised intracranial pressure.\nCondition\nMedicine\nCodes\nAdult dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nSpinal Cord\nCompression\ndexamethasone\niv\nB\nV\n16mg\nstat\nstat dose\nand refer\nOr\nprednisolone po\nB\nV\n30-60mg\nonce a day\n10days\nRaised\nintracranial\npressure\ndexamethasone\niv\nB\nV\n12-16mg\nonce a day\nreview\nOr\nprednisolone po\nB\nV\n90-120mg once a day\nreview\nOther\nconditions\ndexamethasone\niv\nB\nV\n4-8mg\nonce a day\nreview\nOr\nprednisolone po\nB\nV\n5-20mg\nonce a day\nreview\nReduce dose of steroids progressively to minimal maintenance level once clinical\nimprovement occurs\nAnti-depressants and Neuroleptics\nThese are useful in the treatment of neuropathic (nerve) pain which can be\nassociated with the following conditions among others e.g. Trigeminal Neuralgia,\nPost Herpetic Neuralgia & Peripheral Neuralgia, nerve compression etc.\nMedicine\nCodes\nAdult dose\nFrequency\nDuration\ncarbamazepine\npo\nB\nV\n100mg\n1-2 times a day\nincreasing every\n3 days\nto max of 400mg\n3 times a day,\nreview\nor amitriptyline\npo\nB\nV\n25 - 75mg\nnocte\nreview\nor gabapentin po\nB\nE\n300-1200mg\n1-3 times a day\n(initial dose\n300mg per day)\nreview\n*In severe cases specific nerve block may be needed (using local anaesthetic\nor neurolytic agents)\n*Phantom limb pain can be treated as above. If severe, nerve block may be\nrequired."
