        "shortTitle": "Section 7",
        "longTitle": "MANAGEMENT OF PAIN IN CHILDREN",
        "text": "MANAGEMENT OF PAIN IN CHILDREN\nSee also the section in the Cancer module.\nPain in children needs careful and regular assessment as children may not\ncomplain of pain. Babies also experience pain and may require analgesics.\nParents are good judges of their child’s pain.\nWhen available/ necessary suppositories should be used.\nIf pain is intractable refer for specialist management e.g. regional block or\nwound infiltration or palliative sedation\nInfants < 6 months of age require lower initial opioid dosing, approximately 25-\n50% of the opioid doses provided.\nUtilize developmentally appropriate symptom assessment tools to determine\npresence and severity of pain.\nCurrent WHO analgesic ladder for children has 2 steps (mild and severe). Mild\nopioids (codeine and tramadol) containing medicines are not encouraged in\nchronic pain control in children <12 years due to hepatic insufficiency.\nIn reference to codeine:\noIn the foetus, CYP2D6 activity is absent or less than 1% of adult values. It\nincreases after birth, but it is estimated to be no higher than 25% of the\nadult values in children below five years. Therefore, the analgesic effect\nis (very) low or absent in neonates and young children.\noPercentage of poor metabolizers can vary in ethnic groups from 1% to 30%,\nresulting in ineffectiveness in large numbers of patients, including\nchildren.\nConversely, individuals who metabolize codeine quickly and extensively are at\nrisk of severe opioid toxicity, given the high and uncontrolled conversion of\ncodeine into morphine.\nIn reference to tramadol:\n●there is currently no available evidence for its comparative effectiveness and\nsafety in children.\nMild Pain\nMedicine\nCodes\nPaed dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nparacetamol po\nC\nN\n10-15mg/kg\nevery 4hrs\nreview\nModerate Pain (only for children >12yrs for chronic pain control)\nMedicine\nCodes\nPaed dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nor\nparacetamol po\nparacetamol pr\nC\nC\nN\nN\n10-15mg/kg\n10-15mg/kg\nevery 4hrs\nevery 4-6hours\nreview\nreview\nand\ncodeine*\nphosphate\npo\nB\nE\n0.5-1mg/kg\nevery 4hrs\nreview"
