        "text": "*Prevent constipation by increased fluid intake and high fibre diet where\nfeasible and laxative regimen\nSevere Pain\nMedicine\nCodes\nPaed dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nparacetamol\npo/pr\nC\nN\n10-15mg/kg\nevery 4hrs\nreview\nand\nmorphine po\nB\nV\n<6 months =\n0.02mg/kg\n>6months =\n0.04mg/kg\nevery 4hrs\nor\nmorphine sc/iv B\nV\n0.025 mg/kg\nper 4 hours as continuous sc/iv\ninfusion\nN.B morphine syrup is encouraged in children especially infants and in adults\nwith difficulties in swallowing tablets. Suppositories can also be used in this\nsituation\nNausea and vomiting\nMedicine\nCodes\nPaed dose\nFrequency\nDuration\nmetoclopramide po\nC\nN\n0.1-\n0.2mg/kg\n3 times a day\nreview\nor\npromethazine po*\nB\nN\n0.025-\n0.05mg/kg\n3 times a day\nreview\n*not for use in children under the age of 2yrs\nCARE\nOF\nOTHER\nCOMMON\nPALLIATIVE\nCARE\nSYMPTOMS\nIN\nCHILDREN AND ADULTS\nGIT\nNausea and vomiting\nMetoclopramide – see above under pain management\nProchloperazine – see above under pain management\nHaloperidol – see above under pain management\nCNS"
