        "text": "OPIODS\nMorphine\nMedicine\nCodes\nDose\nmorphine im\nB\nV\n0.1-0.2mg/kg 4hrly PRN\nIndications\nModerate to severe Postoperative pain\nPatient Controlled Analgesia (PCA) using intravenous infusion\nPreservative free morphine for epidural infusions (refer to local protocols).\nCaution/Side Effects\nPatient should be closely monitored for side effects mainly respiratory\ndepression\nPruritis\nNausea and Vomiting\nConstipation\nUrinary retention\nPethidine\nFor mild to moderate acute postoperative pain\nMedicine\nCodes\nDose\nOnset\nDuration\npethidine im\nB\nV\n1-2mg/kg\n3 hourly\nor\ntramadol im/iv\nB\nV\n50mg -100mg 4 -6hrly/m\nor\ntramadol po\nB\nV\n50-100mg 4 -6hrly\nreview\nIndications\nMild to Moderate Acute Post-operative pain\nFentanyl\nA synthetic phenylpiperidine derivative opiod analgesic\nMedicine\nCodes\nDose\nOnset\nDuration\nfentanyl inj\nS\nN\n1-10mcg/kg"
